data: {"delta":{"partial_json":"{\"file_path\": \"/home/<USER:1>/.local/share/cs-campaign/output/mission-summary.md\", \"content\": \"# Campaign csrclkey — mission summary\\n\\n## Mission\\nDeliver `src/greet.py` with `greet(name)` returning `\\\"Hello, \u003cname\u003e!\\\"` and\\n`tests/test_greet.py` covering a normal name and the empty string, with\\n`python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` exiting 0.\\n\\n## Outcome: campaign-met\\n\\nAll three stated criteria are satisfied, verified independently by the\\norchestrator (not just by dev's report):\\n\\n- `src/greet.py` (dev branch `cs-sandbox/<DEV:1>.<GROUP:1>`,\\n  commit `46e2e8f`):\\n  ```\\n  def greet(name):\\n      return f\\\"Hello, {name}!\\\"\\n  ```\\n- `tests/test_greet.py` contains `unittest` cases for `greet(\\\"World\\\")` -\u003e\\n  `\\\"Hello, World!\\\"` and `greet(\\\"\\\")` -\u003e `\\\"Hello, !\\\"`.\\n- Orchestrator fetched dev's branch (`cs-campaign-member fetch dev subject`),\\n  checked it out into an isolated git worktree, and ran\\n  `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` directly: 2 tests ran, result `OK`,\\n  exit code 0.\\n\\n## Process\\n- dev's initial briefing dispatch (d001) was reviewed and accepted.\\n- Single work dispatch (d002) sent to dev with exact requirements (file\\n  paths, function behavior, test coverage, verification command, branch/\\n  scope constraints).\\n- dev implemented both files in one pass, ran the tests itself, and\\n  committed only `src/greet.py` and `tests/test_greet.py` to its own branch.\\n- Orchestrator judged by fetching and independently re-running the tests\\n  (not by trusting dev's report alone) before accepting.\\n\\n## Orchestrator's own branch\\nThe orchestrator role is judge/dispatcher only (\\\"you run this campaign and\\njudge it; you write no code yourself\\\" — roles brief). No source changes were\\nmade on the orchestrator's branch; the deliverable lives on dev's branch,\\nwhich was fetched and verified as above.\\n\"}","type":"input_json_delta"},"index":1,"type":"content_block_delta"}

